{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d6ff904a-3eaf-465e-a184-488b4f21631a","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Torque measures how strongly a force turns a lever about its pivot. Start with a horizontal lever.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Torque: turning effect"},{"op":"diagram","id":"lever","region":"right","primitives":[{"kind":"line","points":[[0.15,0.55],[0.85,0.55]],"stroke":"solid","meaning":"rigid lever rotating about its left pivot"},{"kind":"point","at":[0.15,0.55],"label":"pivot"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.1,0.65],[0.15,0.57],[0.2,0.65],[0.1,0.65]],"stroke":"solid","meaning":"fixed support beneath the pivot"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d6ff904a-3eaf-465e-a184-488b4f21631a","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Push downward at the far end. The force turns the lever clockwise; its distance from the pivot matters.","ops":[{"op":"arrow","id":"force","canvas_id":"lever","from":[0.85,0.55],"to":[0.85,0.86],"stroke":"solid","label":"F = 10 N"},{"op":"line","id":"distance","canvas_id":"lever","from":[0.15,0.43],"to":[0.85,0.43],"stroke":"dashed","label":"r = 0.5 m"},{"op":"equation","id":"torque","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\tau=rF\\quad\\text{(perpendicular force)}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d6ff904a-3eaf-465e-a184-488b4f21631a","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Multiply ten newtons by half a meter: five newton-meters of clockwise torque.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"answer","anchor":{"el":"torque","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\tau=(0.5\\,\\mathrm{m})(10\\,\\mathrm{N})=5\\,\\mathrm{N\\,m}"},{"op":"angle_arc","id":"rotation","canvas_id":"lever","center":[0.15,0.55],"radius":0.23,"start_deg":5,"end_deg":65,"stroke":"solid","label":"clockwise"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d6ff904a-3eaf-465e-a184-488b4f21631a","step":{"id":"s4","script":"The same force applied halfway along produces half the torque. Generally, only the perpendicular component of force causes turning.","ops":[{"op":"arrow","id":"nearforce","canvas_id":"lever","from":[0.5,0.55],"to":[0.5,0.86],"stroke":"dashed","label":"same F"},{"op":"equation","id":"halfresult","anchor":{"el":"answer","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"r=0.25\\,\\mathrm{m}\\ \\Rightarrow\\ \\tau=2.5\\,\\mathrm{N\\,m}"},{"op":"equation","id":"general","anchor":{"el":"halfresult","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\tau=rF\\sin\\theta"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"With the same perpendicular force, what happens to torque if the distance from the pivot doubles?","expected_gist":"The torque doubles."}}}
